DECISIONS kicom
DECISION D001 status=accepted title="HTTPS/KCL instead of direct shell"
DECISION D006 status=accepted title="Persist canonical project memory on KiCom"
DECISION D015 status=accepted title="Living Architecture separates genome, memory and phenotype"
DECISION D018 status=accepted title="No hard delete for Goal/ChatGPT memory history; archive or supersede instead"
DECISION D019 status=accepted title="Use a broad bounded Autonomy Envelope instead of per-operation admin approval"
RATIONALE D019 "Frequent low-risk approvals create human fatigue; boundaries should be defined once and enforced in code"
DECISION D020 status=accepted title="Use FreeOTP as the Human Authorization Bridge for trust-boundary crossings"
RATIONALE D020 "A short-lived human factor can authorize exact RED, production or kernel transactions directly from chat"
DECISION D021 status=accepted title="Use rolling one-time session tokens"
RATIONALE D021 "A token visible in transport logs is already spent after the request that used it"
DECISION D022 status=accepted title="Make GitHub optional only"
RATIONALE D022 "KiCom source reads, update upload, archive and primary feed must work on first-party infrastructure"
DECISION D023 status=accepted title="Treat kicomarchive as append-only release history"
RATIONALE D023 "Install/update packages, source snapshots, hashes and metadata must remain reconstructable"
DECISION D015 status=accepted title="Buffer large chat transactions inertly and rotate the main session only at commit"
RATIONALE D015 "Avoid URL and roundtrip overhead without granting fragment tokens any project-mutation authority"
DECISION D016 status=accepted title="Let exact RED approvals survive session idle for one hour"
RATIONALE D016 "A prepared binding remains hash- and state-bound; execution still requires a fresh one-use TOTP and binding revalidation"
END_DECISIONS kicom
